llama-3.3-70b-versatile,Female,College graduate/some postgrad,Moderate,20,1,"I select this option because I believe nuclear power can provide a reliable source of energy and help meet increasing demand, and its low-carbon footprint can also help reduce greenhouse gas emissions, which I see as a practical benefit despite not being an environmentalist.",2,"The preservation of existing infrastructure is favored to ensure a stable, reliable energy supply and avoid the high capital costs and taxpayer burdens of building new facilities.","While preserving existing infrastructure may seem cost-effective, I believe that investing in new nuclear power facilities is necessary to meet growing energy demands and reduce our reliance on outdated, inefficient systems. By building new facilities, we can take advantage of advancements in nuclear technology and safety features, ultimately providing a more reliable and sustainable energy supply in the long run.","Renewable energy sources, energy efficiency, and storage technologies are considered safer, cleaner, and more sustainable alternatives that provide energy security without the long-term liabilities or geopolitical dependencies inherent to nuclear power.","While I understand the appeal of renewable energy sources, I still believe that nuclear power is a more reliable and efficient option for meeting our increasing energy demands, and its benefits outweigh the potential drawbacks. Additionally, I think it's unrealistic to assume that we can solely rely on renewables, efficiency, and storage to meet our energy needs, at least not in the near future, which is why I think nuclear power should be a key part of our energy mix."
