qwen/qwen3-32b,Female,College graduate/some postgrad,Liberal,100,3,"While nuclear power is low-carbon, I prioritize the long-term risks of nuclear waste and potential accidents, which is why I support phasing it out in favor of safer, renewable alternatives.",1,Safety and waste management concerns are perceived as manageable through modern technological advancements and proper regulatory oversight.,"I appreciate the optimism about technology and regulation, but we have to ask ourselves: can we truly guarantee safety over the centuries that nuclear waste will need to be stored, or prevent human error and geopolitical conflicts from compromising these systems? Renewable energy, by contrast, doesn’t saddle us with such long-term liabilities.","Risks related to safety and waste management are regarded as manageable through modern engineering advancements, strict regulatory oversight, and innovative disposal solutions, especially when compared to the catastrophic consequences of global climate collapse.","I appreciate the emphasis on technological progress, but I remain skeptical about whether any system—no matter how advanced—can completely eliminate the risks of nuclear accidents or ensure the secure, long-term storage of radioactive waste. My priority is investing in truly sustainable, inherently safe energy sources that don’t carry the potential for irreversible harm."
